<header class="hero"><p class="eyebrow">THE DARK CODEX / ACTIVE DIRECTORY</p><h1>NetExec<span>.</span></h1><p class="lead">SMB, LDAP, and WinRM authentication and enumeration. NetExec (nxc) provides a consistent interface for authenticated network-service checks across Windows environments.</p></header>
<img class="hero-img" src="/images/dark-codex/netexec.png" alt="NetExec Dark Codex cover" loading="eager" width="768" height="256" />
<div class="note"><strong>Scope:</strong> These examples are intended for systems you own or are explicitly authorized to assess. Replace placeholders with lab values. CLI options can change between releases; check each tool's <code>--help</code> output.</div>
<div class="body-grid"><article>
<section class="section" id="commands"><p class="eyebrow">01 / FIELD COMMANDS</p><h2>Commands you'll actually use</h2><div class="examples"><div class="example"><h3>SMB connectivity</h3><p>Check SMB reachability and host metadata.</p><pre><code>nxc smb &lt;target&gt;</code></pre></div><div class="example"><h3>Validate authorized credentials</h3><p>Test supplied credentials against SMB.</p><pre><code>nxc smb &lt;target&gt; -u &lt;user&gt; -p &lt;password&gt;</code></pre></div><div class="example"><h3>List shares</h3><p>Enumerate shares accessible to the account.</p><pre><code>nxc smb &lt;target&gt; -u &lt;user&gt; -p &lt;password&gt; --shares</code></pre></div><div class="example"><h3>List domain users</h3><p>Query domain users via LDAP when permitted.</p><pre><code>nxc ldap &lt;dc-ip&gt; -u &lt;user&gt; -p &lt;password&gt; --users</code></pre></div><div class="example"><h3>WinRM access check</h3><p>Check whether credentials work with WinRM.</p><pre><code>nxc winrm &lt;target&gt; -u &lt;user&gt; -p &lt;password&gt;</code></pre></div><div class="example"><h3>Protocol help</h3><p>Inspect modules and flags supported by your build.</p><pre><code>nxc smb --help</code></pre></div></div></section>
<section class="section" id="concepts"><p class="eyebrow">02 / REMEMBER THIS</p><h2>Key concepts and flags</h2><div class="terms"><div class="term"><strong>Protocols</strong><p>smb, ldap, winrm select the service you want to query.</p></div><div class="term"><strong>Credentials</strong><p>-u and -p supply account credentials; avoid saving real passwords in notes.</p></div><div class="term"><strong>Permissions</strong><p>A successful login does not imply administrative rights.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="section" id="workflow"><p class="eyebrow">03 / FIELD NOTES</p><h2>Practical reminders</h2><ul><li>Use only accounts and hosts within your authorized lab scope.</li><li>A blocked LDAP port is a network constraint, not evidence that no domain exists.</li></ul></section>
<section class="section sources" id="sources"><p class="eyebrow">04 / SOURCES & CREDITS</p><h2>Documentation and attribution</h2><p>This is an independently written PentestBlueprint quick reference informed by the official project documentation below. Tool names and trademarks belong to their respective projects; no affiliation or endorsement is implied.</p><ul><li><a href="https://github.com/Pennyw0rth/NetExec" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NetExec project ↗</a></li><li><a href="https://www.netexec.wiki/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NetExec documentation ↗</a></li></ul></section>
</article><aside class="toc" aria-label="On this page"><strong>ON THIS PAGE</strong><a href="#commands">Common commands</a><a href="#concepts">Key concepts</a><a href="#workflow">Field reminders</a><a href="#sources">Sources & credits</a></aside></div>
